__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
findings.jsonl
*.local.json
# …and the atomic-write temp files that sit NEXT to them. `*.local.json` does not match
# `settings.local.json.tmp.598784.babbe3fedad7` — the suffix comes after the extension — so a
# `git add -A` racing a settings write commits one. That happened on this branch (harmless
# content, a local permission allowlist), and the same shape of near miss is what §G5 hardened
# the capture rules against: an ignore rule that looks like it covers a class but matches one
# filename spelling of it.
*.local.json.tmp.*
.DS_Store

# Real capture data — prompt-bearing, never committed (see DECISIONS.md "Gemini adapter" §G3/G5).
# `fixtures/` is the private v1 Claude run; the acceptance test skips when it is absent. It was
# NOT previously ignored, so a stray `git add -A` in a working tree that had it would have
# recommitted the data that was deliberately scrubbed out of this repo.
/fixtures/
/fixtures-gemini/
telemetry*.jsonl
*.telemetry.jsonl
*.ausearch
/capture/
